246
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:48,510
You didn't say, "Boutros Boutros-Ghali."

247
00:14:48,670 --> 00:14:50,720
Boutros Boutros-Ghali.

248
00:14:53,050 --> 00:14:54,220
He says he was too.

249
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:56,310
Interesting.

250
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:59,770
Uh, so I was wondering...

251
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,810
Before you get all talky again...

252
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:05,480
...um, could you also please tell Sergei...

253
00:15:05,650 --> 00:15:09,280
...that I really like his suit.

254
00:15:22,830 --> 00:15:25,750
Uh, he said, "Thank you very much. You look very pretty tonight.

255
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,340
Your hair, golden like the sun." So you're a chef?

256
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:32,220
I'm also thinking of opening up my own restaurant.

257
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,890
- Oh, really?     - Monica...

258
00:15:34,050 --> 00:15:36,010
...could I talk to you behind my menu, please?

259
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:42,390
- What are you doing?     - Well, I was having a conversation.

260
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:44,270
Yeah, but Mischa's so interested in you...

261
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:47,230
...that Sergei and I haven't been able to say two words to each other.

262
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,990
What do you want me to do? Sit here while the three of you have a conversation?

263
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:52,860
That would be great. Thank you.

264
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:03,330
- Hello?     - Oh, hi. It's Mark.

265
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:06,750
What? Is it my breath?

266
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:10,670
No. Sorry. I just thought you were somebody else. Hi.

267
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,680
Hi, well, look, I was just gonna leave a message.

268
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,510
Isn't tonight your anniversary dinner?

269
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,430
Rach? Are you okay?

270
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,770
Yeah, I'm fine.

271
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:25,350
You wanna talk? I mean, I can come over.

272
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,230
No, really, no. Please. That's okay.

273
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,650
All right. I'm coming over and I'm bringing Chinese food.

274
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:33,280
- Oh, yeah, I'm not hungry.     - It's for me.

275
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:37,410
Okay. Bye.

276
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,830
- So, what'll you do?     - What can I do?

277
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:45,330
One person wants to break up, you break up.

278
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:49,250
Hey, no way. Come on, this is you guys. Call her and work it out.

279
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:52,630
Come on. We just had this huge fight. Don't I have to wait a while?

280
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:57,220
Hey, this isn't like swimming after you eat. Pick up your phone.

281
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:03,980
You know that whole swimming thing is a myth.

282
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:06,690
Yeah, tell that to my Uncle Lenny.

283
00:17:06,850 --> 00:17:08,980
Why? What happened to him?

284
00:17:09,150 --> 00:17:12,280
Nothing. He just really believes in that.

285
00:17:13,690 --> 00:17:17,110
Ugh. And then we got into this big, stupid fight... It was awful.

286
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:21,910
I told him he treats me like a park ranger, something, ugh...

287
00:17:22,950 --> 00:17:24,410
And then...

288
00:17:25,330 --> 00:17:27,830
...I told him I wanted to take a break.

289
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,210
I don't want to take a break.

290
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:32,420
Well, I'm sorry.

291
00:17:33,590 --> 00:17:36,510
- Egg roll?     - No.

292
00:17:37,430 --> 00:17:40,430
And then I called him, and he wasn't there.

293
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,260
He's probably just out.

294
00:17:42,430 --> 00:17:45,480
Oh, thank you. That's very helpful. I'm glad you came over.

295
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:52,610
- Hello?     - Hi, it's me.

296
00:17:53,150 --> 00:17:56,490
- Hi. Oh, I'm so glad you called.     - Really?

297
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:59,990
I've been thinking this is crazy. Don't you think we can work on this?

298
00:18:00,990 --> 00:18:02,700
Hey, what do you want to drink?

299
00:18:02,990 --> 00:18:04,040
Who's that?

300
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:07,120
Nobody?

301
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:10,330
Is it okay if I finish the apple juice?

302
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,090
Is that Mark?

303
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:17,050
- Ooh, honey, look, he just came over...     - Yeah, got it.

304
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:25,100
Hey, Dinosaur Guy. Look at you, so sad.

305
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:28,020
- Come dance.     - Uh, that's okay. Thanks.

306
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:29,560
Hey.

307
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:32,520
You don't have to smile. You just have to dance.

308
00:18:32,690 --> 00:18:35,780
Look, I don't feel like dancing. I feel like having a drink, okay?

309
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:38,530
Oh, okay. Hey, two beers.

310
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,700
And the vet said it was time.

311
00:18:42,870 --> 00:18:44,700
And so from half-a-world away...

312
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:47,910
...while my mother held the phone to his ear...

313
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:51,120
...I said goodbye to my dog...

314
00:18:51,290 --> 00:18:53,330
...in seven languages.

315
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:57,590
- Could I have a tissue?     - Oh, yeah, sure.

316
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:00,800
I just hope you don't accidentally suck it up through your nose...

317
00:19:00,970 --> 00:19:02,640
...and choke on it.

318
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:12,350
Ugh. Sergei would like to apologize for my behavior tonight.

319
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:16,110
Well, tell him, "Apology accepted."

320
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:23,410
He's unbelievable. For the first time in three years, someone wants to talk to me.

321
00:19:23,570 --> 00:19:26,990
But do you think he would let me enjoy that? No.

322
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:31,210
You silly diplomat. Why don't you learn some English, Sergei?

323
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:36,880
Excuse me, but, um, ahem, isn't he paying for your dinner?

324
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,050
Hey, the man's dog just died.

325
00:19:57,150 --> 00:19:59,440
I have just resigned my post.

326
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:01,860
Would you care to accompany me to the Rainbow Room?

327
00:20:02,030 --> 00:20:03,780
I have diplomatic coupons.

328
00:20:06,530 --> 00:20:08,530
It would be my pleasure.

329
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:11,410
My guy has coupons.

330
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:16,040
Your guy can't even say "coupons."

331
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:24,090
Uh, plate.

332
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:26,760
- Plate. Yes. Plate. Plate.     - Plate. Plate.

333
00:20:27,470 --> 00:20:28,640
Plate.

334
00:20:30,310 --> 00:20:32,100
See, we don't need them.

335
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,190
Plate?

336
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,900
Yeah.

337
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:43,490
# Sleight of hand And twist of fate #

338
00:20:43,650 --> 00:20:47,110
# On a bed of nails She makes me wait #

339
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,030
I like this song.

340
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:52,160
Well, you're practically dancing already.

341
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:56,330
- Why don't you just do it over here?     - Oh, no.

342
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:58,710
What are you, married?

343
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,840
Because that's okay.

344
00:21:15,770 --> 00:21:18,600
Oh, be home, be home, be home...

345
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,320
Be home, be home, be home.

346
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:26,530
You're not home.

347
00:21:32,950 --> 00:21:36,750
# With or without you #

348
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:38,830
Still no smile?

349
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:54,680
# And you give yourself away #

350
00:21:54,850 --> 00:21:59,150
# And you give #

351
00:21:59,310 --> 00:22:02,770
# And you give yourself away #

352
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:18,370
American.

353
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:20,420
- American.     - American.

354
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:23,500
American. You know, it's a very hard language.

355
00:22:24,630 --> 00:22:25,670
Let's do it again.

